{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic","id":845544,"title":"Delerium and Rationality or Logic...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-11T03:30:01-08:00","id":845544,"title":"Delerium and Rationality or Logic...","content":"Reading Call to battle, It trys explaining the Delerium as a product of humans faith in logic and science, Saw same thing in &quot;Wyrm Wolf&quot; Since I never read original printing, of WTA 1st Edition, was this there? Was the Impergium Retconned into the settings history to help it make sense? <br /> <br /> I Thought &quot;wait, they go into a fit, when they see the impossible, even those who ALLREADY KNOW academicly werewolves are real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:15:57-08:00","id":845552,"title":"","content":"The Delirium has pretty consistently been portrayed as racial memories (what ever that exactly mean) of the terrors inflicted upon the humans by the Shifters during the Impergium. Fiction has never been particularly sensible or well read on the actual topics of the games, and it should never be referenced as factual information. Besides it came out after 2nd ed, so it's not &quot;an older source&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:55:33-08:00","id":845578,"title":"","content":"wanted to ask... reactions on the chart of &quot;Disbelief&quot; What happens when the person KNOWS academicly that Werewolves are real","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:24:10-08:00","id":845589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845578#post845578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wanted to ask... reactions on the chart of &quot;Disbelief&quot; What happens when the person KNOWS academicly that Werewolves are real</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you even know that Werewolves are academically real? If you suffer from disbelief, you believe that it was a hoax, that you were drugged, that it was animatronics, or that it was a prank of some sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:33:32-08:00","id":845594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845578#post845578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wanted to ask... reactions on the chart of &quot;Disbelief&quot; What happens when the person KNOWS academicly that Werewolves are real</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, those novels are both old, and tend to do their own canon.<br /> <br /> Second, it doesn't matter. If the person has a very strong willpower, then. But otherwise Delirium will affect them just the same. It is one thing to know a werewolf exists and another to face one in person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:51:18-08:00","id":845609,"title":"","content":"In the game mechanics, there is no rules for that. Unless the person is kin or supernatural, Delirium always hits. However, there was a reference in 2nd Edition, that certain groups who are per se more in tune with the supernatural, the Delirium might not be as effective. Native americans were an example. And, iirc, the rural asian population was described as being aware of the supernatural, but considering them an anathema so they don't talk about them and ignore their doings.<br /> <br /> From 2nd edition:<br /> <b>The Delirium</b>: Garou in Crinos form create a blind, instinctive terror in humans who view them. Humans' dependence upon rationality is so total that they cannot accept the truth of werewolves' existence; they will believe any convenient rationale ra ther than concede the existence of Garou. Most simply forget what they have seen. The end result of this reaction, known as the Veil, is the predominant reason why werewolves are generally thought to be creatures of legend.<br /> <br /> I always found that the Delirium as a means of staying sane on the humans part made more sense, then an millenia old fear inherited in humans.<br /> Several questions remain unanswered: Are children, toddlers, infants immune ?<br /> Will repeated exposure in a short time frame drive one insane or lead to immunity ?<br /> Are sorcerers and ghouls immune ?<br /> Are already insane people immune ?<br /> <br /> Also, I found that the &quot;the impergium is the reason&quot; statement made more sense if it was the Children of Gaia blaming the other garou, rather than an out-of-character game book statement. But then again, I still hate the &quot;human as cattle and lower race&quot; statements in revised, as opposed to a sheppard culling the herd like it was described in 2nd. One makes all your ancestors look like wyrm-worshipping douchs, the other looks like a function that needed to be taken, to keep the planet in balance...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:05:36-08:00","id":845857,"title":"","content":"What about the gift &quot;Terror of the Dire Wolf&quot; What to do with &quot;Disbelief&quot; then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:12:34-08:00","id":845859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845857#post845857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the gift &quot;Terror of the Dire Wolf&quot; What to do with &quot;Disbelief&quot; then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics for the Delirium are also used for what happens when humans see other pants-shittingly frightening sights, such as Nexus Crawlers or possessed with the Horror power. Neither of these participated in the Impergium, though for an interesting twist in an individual campaign, you can have it so that the Garou and Fera were set up in the ancient times, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T19:03:48-08:00","id":845917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845609#post845609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several questions remain unanswered: Are children, toddlers, infants immune ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would children be immune?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845609#post845609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will repeated exposure in a short time frame drive one insane or lead to immunity ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Project Twilight, it's stated that at Storyteller discretion, certain important characters (particularly non-Garou Player Characters), should be given a cumulative increase on their effective Willpower score when attempting to determine the effects of Delerium with each additional exposure. I seem to remember that this was considered the exception, not the rule as PCs are assumed to be exceptional in some way, and that repeated exposure to most &quot;ordinary&quot; humans would result in permanent insanity (although I don't recall any actual mechanics being published for this anywhere).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T20:13:45-08:00","id":845926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845917#post845917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would children be immune?<br /> <br /> In Project Twilight, it's stated that at Storyteller discretion, certain important characters (particularly non-Garou Player Characters), should be given a cumulative increase on their effective Willpower score when attempting to determine the effects of Delerium with each additional exposure. I seem to remember that this was considered the exception, not the rule as PCs are assumed to be exceptional in some way, and that repeated exposure to most &quot;ordinary&quot; humans would result in permanent insanity (although I don't recall any actual mechanics being published for this anywhere).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the high-difficulty Wits + Occult support roll; every success pushes you up a point from your normal rating for the purposes of resisting the Delirium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T03:12:55-08:00","id":846013,"title":"","content":"I think that if you had a human who knew for a fact that werewolves existed and saw one, that he or she would suffer from the temporary effects of the delirium but would not necessarily try to reason away the werewolf because they know that those creatures exist. I do, however, think that their memories of the incident might be hazy and hard to recollect accurately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:33:43-07:00","id":847024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845917#post845917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would children be immune?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a statement that spooked around in LARP games for a while a decade ago, or so.<br /> The reasoning was something like that kids are still open to the supernatural and can see monsters everywhere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:54:12-07:00","id":847030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847024#post847024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a statement that spooked around in LARP games for a while a decade ago, or so.<br /> The reasoning was something like that kids are still open to the supernatural and can see monsters everywhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really supported by the rules, though. And just because they are children doesn't meant the primordial terror that the shifters inspire is any lesser. I think it's bleeding from Mage and Changeling there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T06:50:30-07:00","id":847046,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and probably also the idea that children might be immune to Obfuscate (which was also a statement that was popular in LARPs a decade or more ago).<br /> <br /> Anyways, there is a mention in 2nd Edition, that people who are more in tune with the natural world, might have more resistance to the delirium.<br /> <br /> I don't have access to my books right now, but the statement:<br /> <i>&quot;Members of cultures that didn\u2019t suffer the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Impergium\" target=\"_blank\">Impergium</a> to a great degree (such as Native Americans and Aboriginal Australians) might also be granted a bonus to resist Delirium \u2014 though only if they\u2019ve been raised without contact with other cultures.&quot;</i><br /> ...can be found on whitewolf wika.<br /> <br /> So the thought might have risen from the assumption, that children, who haven't been raised yet, in general would be granted such benefits.<br /> Also, in a classical culling, like the impergium pre-revised, the old and weak were in danger, not the children (unless sick).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T07:10:17-07:00","id":847053,"title":"","content":"I think that's just bad writing. They talk about cultures who were spared the worst excesses. We're talking about let's say the tribes in the area around the Siberakh, or maybe certain tribes in the territory of the Uktena and the Croatan. The idea behind that text is that if you come from those people as your major genetic (spiritual?) contribution, that you might have higher delirium resistance.<br /> <br /> If it was about being raised, then you'd be immune from Werewolves if your parents never told you about Werewolves, and that's patent nonsense and counter to the spirit of the Delirium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T07:44:17-07:00","id":847060,"title":"","content":"Yeah...<br /> <br /> Still, I prefer a subconscious self-protection of the rational mind - that might not fully work - over an inherited fear cased by beasts who slaughtered humans more then ten millennia ago.<br /> <br /> Then again, I find culling the weak and sick amongst the humans as Impergium more appealing than enslaving them as a race of lesser worth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:10:00-07:00","id":847160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847060#post847060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...<br /> Still, I prefer a subconscious self-protection of the rational mind - that might not fully work - over an inherited fear cased by beasts who slaughtered humans more then ten millennia ago.<br /> <br /> Then again, I find culling the weak and sick amongst the humans as Impergium more appealing than enslaving them as a race of lesser worth...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really depends on who is telling the story. Your view is as supported as the more popular decimation policy. I think we'll get the first truly official view with Shattered Dreams very soon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:33:08-07:00","id":847180,"title":"","content":"nah... I don't care for what really happened. And with a concept like a fluid past as &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot; has, it is a mood point.<br /> <br /> But I care how it is presented in the core rules as &quot;what garou today believe&quot;. And I have a problem with &quot;We honour our ancestors and the strong lineages ending with us, but starting with the best of the best, the first pack. Beings created by Luna herself to protect her sister gaia - chosen for their virtues like courage, selflessness, as they demonstrated every day by enslaving humans, killing and haunting them for no reason at all, except maybe that they could.&quot;<br /> <br /> Try that speech educating lost cubs in a LARP game while keeping a straight face.... especially if the players are new to the setting, too.<br /> <br /> For me, the garou need to believe that their ancestors were paragons of virtue, that are worthy of their worship even today. And all the questionable elements of their past, like the Impergium or the War of Rage have explanations that don't tarnish that picture. That is possible to accomplish if one attributes these events to either being right at that time, but wrong today, for the world has changed, or a series of misunderstandings and grievances on all parts. But revised has a tone, that I often read as the current garou generation blaming their ancestors from ten millenia ago for a lot of things and picturing them in a way, that is without a doubt wyrmish. And that doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:39:47-07:00","id":847240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847180#post847180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nah... I don't care for what really happened. And with a concept like a fluid past as &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot; has, it is a mood point.<br /> <br /> But I care how it is presented in the core rules as &quot;what garou today believe&quot;. And I have a problem with &quot;We honour our ancestors and the strong lineages ending with us, but starting with the best of the best, the first pack. Beings created by Luna herself to protect her sister gaia - chosen for their virtues like courage, selflessness, as they demonstrated every day by enslaving humans, killing and haunting them for no reason at all, except maybe that they could.&quot;<br /> <br /> Try that speech educating lost cubs in a LARP game while keeping a straight face.... especially if the players are new to the setting, too.<br /> <br /> For me, the garou need to believe that their ancestors were paragons of virtue, that are worthy of their worship even today. And all the questionable elements of their past, like the Impergium or the War of Rage have explanations that don't tarnish that picture. That is possible to accomplish if one attributes these events to either being right at that time, but wrong today, for the world has changed, or a series of misunderstandings and grievances on all parts. But revised has a tone, that I often read as the current garou generation blaming their ancestors from ten millenia ago for a lot of things and picturing them in a way, that is without a doubt wyrmish. And that doesn't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. As much as I always insist on the Garou being heroic, and that they are the &quot;Good&quot; guys, you do have to confess that they have a very long history of being total and utter dicks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:33:25-07:00","id":847278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847240#post847240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. As much as I always insist on the Garou being heroic, and that they are the &quot;Good&quot; guys, you do have to confess that they have a very long history of being total and utter dicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not.<br /> <br /> Like I said, culling the herd - meaning to kill of the old and sick - keeps the herd strong. Humans didn't understand that, while garou have the &quot;Don't suffer thy people to tend for your sickness&quot;-ruling. So, a forced culling amongst human settlements, once they started to settle, made sense for the garou of that time. The humans were given means to avert the natural order (intelligence), so the garou acted accordingly. and according to some sources, the garou didn't even end the Impergium without a plan. The garou should have tried to educate mankind to live in harmony with Gaias other creatures, or so the 'end the Impergium'-fraction hoped. But that plan failed for the tribes in Europe and Asia minor, while Uktena, Wendigo and Croatans had it figured out quite good, until the Wyrmbringers came.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the garou remember that they were made Gaias defenders because Wolf sacrificed himself to save Gaia from the Darkness and was rewarded with resurrection for that, after all other animals had failed and not included him due to his rage. So, when their Champion was murdered in a diplomatic mission to the Gurahl (that arguable the Gurahl should have provided save passage for), they reasonably expected that the Gurahl would resurrect the Champion. But they refused, and provided save haven for the alleged murderer. That the garou frenzied and killed the gurahl is tragic, but doesn't make them dicks. Although, we know that the Bubasti was framed for the murder, but the garou didn't know then and don't know today.<br /> In any case, whenever a pack of garou would meet a member of another changing breed that was wyrm tainted and they would kill that being, others of the same changing breed would if they later discovered the body only find that garou murdered one of their own. That such an action might have been justified is never discussed.<br /> Also, for all that I don't like in revised (and the CoG TB in particular), I like that the Children of Gaia blame themselves for the War of Rage escalating from a isolated incident to an era of mistrust and violence. They, again and again, convinced (with their gifts it is really easy) garou and other changers to meet and end their conflict and every time it blew up in their face. All they managed was to create more reasons for each side to mistrust and hate the other - that is until they stopped and the War of Rage slowly ebbed down.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, what I'm saying is, that the Garou on modern times can very easily paint their pre-historic ancestors in a benevolent light - as they should for they supposedly come from a culture that worships their ancestors. It ain't matter what is true and what is not. It is hard, I'd say outright impossible, to be proud of one's heritage (or people) if it is filled with people who were performing genocide, twice. But since the Setting wants the Garou to be a proud culture, their perception of their peoples past should be presented in a way that allows for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:08:16-07:00","id":847326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847278#post847278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reasoning was something like that kids are still open to the supernatural and can see monsters everywhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh... I think that simply because small children are afraid of the dark and are constantly paranoid that monsters are hiding under their bed / waiting to leap out of their closet -- provides justification that the Delerium should be (if anything) even stronger in children. They might go on and on about a &quot;dog-monster&quot; or something (given that they'd have less intellect to rationalize with), but otherwise I don't see why they would be immune.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847278#post847278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what I'm saying is, that the Garou on modern times can very easily paint their pre-historic ancestors in a benevolent light - as they should for they supposedly come from a culture that worships their ancestors. It ain't matter what is true and what is not. It is hard, I'd say outright impossible, to be proud of one's heritage (or people) if it is filled with people who were performing genocide, twice. But since the Setting wants the Garou to be a proud culture, their perception of their peoples past should be presented in a way that allows for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I actually agree with all of that...<br /> <br /> That said, I think it should be made clear that what the Garou<i> think </i>happened in the past (or what they choose to believe) is not necessarily what actually <i>did</i> happen. And a few tribes (like the CoG, for instance) should still have a contrary opinion on the matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:48:57-07:00","id":847352,"title":"","content":"Oh speaking of Rationality and Logic? Does a Metis whos Deformity is &quot;Insanity&quot; take an honor loss For trying to be collected as its &quot;Trying to hide his Metis deformity&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:15:07-07:00","id":847417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847352#post847352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh speaking of Rationality and Logic? Does a Metis whos Deformity is &quot;Insanity&quot; take an honor loss For trying to be collected as its &quot;Trying to hide his Metis deformity&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They have to be able to get jobs done some time. Also, you can't really will those things away, that's not how they work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:19:33-07:00","id":847418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=847417#post847417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They have to be able to get jobs done some time. Also, you can't really will those things away, that's not how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, that aspect is only in the renown chart.Generally it would make no sense for a metis with beastial reflection to carry a mirror showing that, or metis with silver allergy to carry silver. Nevermind the poor metis with seizures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T03:06:35-07:00","id":861716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic?p=845859#post845859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanics for the Delirium are also used for what happens when humans see other pants-shittingly frightening sights, such as Nexus Crawlers or possessed with the Horror power. Neither of these participated in the Impergium, though for an interesting twist in an individual campaign, you can have it so that the Garou and Fera were set up in the ancient times, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference for that ?","signature":"","edited"